# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Two reasons this file matters here beyond build speed:
#
#  1. `.env` holds a real provider key. The Dockerfile never COPYs it, but an
#     excluded file cannot be leaked by a future COPY either -- keep it out of
#     the context entirely rather than relying on the Dockerfile staying
#     careful.
#  2. `chroma_db/` and `facts.db` are LOCAL ingest output. The image builds its
#     own via `RUN python -m src.ingest` (FR6.2). Shipping the local copies in
#     would upload hundreds of MB and risk a stale index silently shadowing
#     the freshly built one.
#
# NOTE: `data/` is deliberately NOT excluded. The Dockerfile copies it and the
# build-time ingest reads the committed filings from it.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local ingest output — the image builds its own
chroma_db/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
facts.db
traces.sqlite

# VCS and CI
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/

# Tests and docs are not needed at runtime and only invalidate layer caches
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Agent/editor tooling
.claude/
.cursor/
.rocketride/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Compose is for local development, not the image
docker-compose.yml
